{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QuantumEntropy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QuantumEntropy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.MathConstants","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.quantumEntropy_surface_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.quantumEntropy_surface_independent","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-entropy.lean#L44-L54","doc":"Bounding-surface independence (Yekutieli non-abelian Stokes):\nif two bounding surfaces carry the same adjoint-trace flux, the\nquantum entropy agrees on them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.quantumEntropy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.quantumEntropy","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-entropy.lean#L29-L42","doc":"**Quantum entropy** of a region `U ⊆ M`.\n\n`S_q(U) = -tr_Ad ∮_{∂U} ω_F ∧ *η_q`.\n\nThe full surface integral requires the Yekutieli non-abelian\nStokes machinery; here we record its **density**: the entropy is\nthe negated adjoint-trace flux of the operational-entropy density\n`η_q` through the bounding surface.  Modelled as the (region-wise)\nflux value `entropyFlux`, which downstream surface-independence\nlemmas constrain. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-entropy","label":"def:quantum-entropy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-entropy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.R_q","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-entropy.lean#L26-L27","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ). ","signatureChunk":0}]}